W("Name two 'little extras' that Mrs Pumphrey gave Tricki between meals.", 2, "Any two: malt, cod-liver oil, a bowl of Horlicks at night (also cream cakes and chocolates). (1+1)", "E"),
W("What did Tricki look like when Herriot saw him in the street? Answer using the narrator's comparison.", 2, "He had become hugely fat, 'like a bloated sausage with a leg at each corner'; his eyes were bloodshot and rheumy and his tongue lolled from his jaws. (2)", "E"),
W("Why did Mrs Pumphrey say she gave Tricki the extra food?", 2, "She thought he must be suffering from malnutrition because he was listless and had no energy, so she gave him extras to 'build him up'. (2)", "E"),
