 ("h2", "4. Theme and values"),
 ("ul", [
  "**Over-indulgence is not love.** Mrs Pumphrey's affection harms Tricki; real care means discipline.",
  "**Common sense beats medicine.** The cure was diet, exercise and company, not surgery.",
  "**Tact.** Herriot is firm with the owner but gentle, and never makes fun of her to her face.",
  "**Health needs balance** of food, activity and a natural environment.",
  "**Irony in the title:** the credit goes to 'surgery' that never happened."]),
 ("note", "IMPORTANT", "There was **no operation**. The title is Mrs Pumphrey's mistaken phrase. Never write that Herriot operated on Tricki."),
